  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know that per ${ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ change is equivalent to $1.8^{\\circ}$ change in ${ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{F}$.\n$\\therefore 40^{\\circ}$ change on celcius scale will corresponds to $72^{\\circ}$ change on Fahrenheit scale.\nHence option (3)",
